mac/view: build without Vulkan

beddaec5ab ("mac/view: make our view aware of possible transparent
rendering", 2026-01-11) made View.isOpaque look at MetalLayer, which is
defined in video/out/mac/metal_layer.swift — compiled only when Vulkan is
enabled. A cocoa + swift build without Vulkan (ours: the app renders via
the libmpv OpenGL render API) then fails with "cannot find type
'MetalLayer' in scope". Guard the check on the feature flag mpv already
passes to swiftc.

--- a/video/out/mac/view.swift
+++ b/video/out/mac/view.swift
@@ -30,9 +30,11 @@

     override var isOpaque: Bool {
+#if HAVE_VULKAN
         if let metalLayer = layer as? MetalLayer {
             return !metalLayer.isOpaque
         }
+#endif

         return true
     }
